### The whole flow, through the gateway: the way clients use the system.
@gw = http://localhost:8080

### Register
POST {{gw}}/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "alice@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery staple"}

### Log in
# @name login
POST {{gw}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "alice@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery staple"}

### Open a wallet: the owner is whoever the token says
# @name wallet
POST {{gw}}/v1/wallets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"currency": "USD"}

### Deposit
POST {{gw}}/v1/wallets/{{wallet.response.body.id}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: gw-deposit-1

{"amount": 1050, "currency": "USD"}

### Balance
GET {{gw}}/v1/wallets/{{wallet.response.body.id}}/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### Without a token: 401
GET {{gw}}/v1/wallets/{{wallet.response.body.id}}/balance
